From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:12:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] view: Windows open and come to the screen they were picked on

With a second screen (e.g. a virtual one shown over VNC) the user works
on the phone by touch and on the other screen with a pointer. A touch
does not move the cursor, so the cursor does not tell which screen the
user is on. The seat now remembers where the last button press or touch
began, and phoc uses that screen:

- A new window opens there (a dialog on the screen of its parent), also
  when it is maximized or fullscreen from the start, as Firefox restores
  itself; such windows stayed on the screen they were created on.
- A window activated through foreign-toplevel comes there: a task bar on
  the second screen and Phosh's overview on the phone both list all
  windows, picking one brings it to that screen.

Moving reuses the code of move-to-monitor, split out as
phoc_view_move_to_output().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
